etely there but certainly in  terms of avoiding it  you want to make sure that you're  hydrating even if you don't feel thirsty  you want to drink enough fluids and you  don't want to drink things like  caffeine or alcohol or sugary beverages  those things might actually dehydrate  you  other things you might want to think  about doing obviously wearing sunscreen  because sunburn can make you more prone  to  being unable to regulate your  temperature ac  so important even if it's for two to  three hours a day  if you don't have it at home getting to  a public library or a mall where you can  be inside  avoiding cooking with ovens or stoves  that's going to heat up your  house so there are tips and things that  you can do preventively and proactively  well  that was the problem in the pacific  northwest so many people didn't have air  conditioning right yeah  well how fast can it come on tara it can  come on pretty quickly so your  temperature can rise if you're at that  point where you're about to  become a heat stroke patient within 10  to 15 minutes your temperature can go  above 106. and there are certainly  populations that are more  vulnerable so we think about the  extremes of ages  so infants and kids up to four and then  those over 65  those who are on certain chronic  medications like blood pressure  medicines antihistamines diuretics  antidepressants  also those with chronic medical  conditions things like cardiovascular  disease  and people who obviously have to work  outside so really important to pay  attention to those populations very  serious condition but it is preventable  dr terenaro thank you very much
 

